--- Instructions to run teleop----
1. Start a terminal 
2. conda actvate env_isaac
3. Move to IsaacLab dir
4. Paste: sudo ufw allow 47998:48000,48005,48008,48012/udp
sudo ufw allow 48010/tcp
5. start open xr director: docker run -it --rm --name cloudxr-runtime \
    --user $(id -u):$(id -g) \
    --gpus=all \
    -e "ACCEPT_EULA=Y" \
    --mount type=bind,src=$(pwd)/openxr,dst=/openxr \
    -p 48010:48010 \
    -p 47998:47998/udp \
    -p 47999:47999/udp \
    -p 48000:48000/udp \
    -p 48005:48005/udp \
    -p 48008:48008/udp \
    -p 48012:48012/udp \
    nvcr.io/nvidia/cloudxr-runtime:5.0.1
    
 6. New terminal with same env 
 7. Move to Isaac_Lab_Projects/Kuka_Med_7/scripts
 8. source cloudxr_env.sh
 9. python teleop_med7_vr.py --ros --enable_cameras
 10. Once sim is online connect boh vision pro and PC to ur mobile hotspot
 11. Start VR from sim 
 12. Open teleop client app on AVP (last app in menu) then connect and play 
 13. gestures are written in terminal - but in general right hand is tracked to move the pointer around with a quick pinch from lrft hand locks its position and then the distance between your finger and thumb adjusts the line length for pointer and again quick left pinch locks it
 14.  ros2 topic echo /surgical_plan/probe_pose
ros2 topic echo /surgical_plan/guide_line
Publishes both pose pose and the line waypoints which can be sunscribed -> these topics publish only when the positino is locked 
